{"case_id":"T8047","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry-point","state-machine","input-semantics","configuration/backend"],"confidence":97,"affected_functions":["h2o_timer_wheel_init","h2o_timer_add_","h2o_timer_add","h2o_timer_del","h2o_timer_wheel__run_","h2o_timer_wheel_run","h2o_timer_wheel_get_wake_at","cascade","compute_slot","timer_wheel","timer_slot"],"reason":"H0 reaches timers only indirectly through HTTP processing on the EPOLL event loop, with mostly fixed timeout values and wall-clock progression. It cannot fuzz the new timer-wheel API as a stateful protocol or control absolute and relative expiration values, run timestamps, add/delete ordering, repeated scheduling, wheel cascading, expired-queue behavior, or the maximum-range rejection path. It also hard-codes H2O_USE_EPOLL=1, leaving the H2O_USE_LIBUV implementation of h2o_timer_add and h2o_timer_del uncovered.","evidence":["H0 defines H2O_USE_EPOLL 1 and drives only h2o_evloop_run(ctx.loop, 10), so it does not instantiate the H2O_USE_LIBUV branch in lib/common/timer.c.","The fuzz bytes Data and Size are used only as HTTP/1 or HTTP/2 socket input through create_accepted; they are never decoded into h2o_timer_abs_t, h2o_timer_val_t, or explicit timer operations.","H0 fixes config.http2.idle_timeout, config.http1.req_timeout, and proxy_config.io_timeout at 10 * 1000, while proxy connect_timeout and first_byte_timeout are fixed at zero; the fuzzer cannot vary these timer values.","h2o_timer_add_ contains input-sensitive behavior for abs_expire <= w->last_run and rejects distances greater than 0xffffffff, but H0 has no entry point that supplies abs_expire or controls w->last_run.","h2o_timer_wheel__run_ selects wheels using timer_wheel(abs_wtime, now), moves ranges of slots, invokes cascade, and executes callbacks from todo and expired lists; H0 cannot generate arbitrary now sequences or timer populations to exercise these state transitions.","The public declarations in include/h2o/timer.h expose h2o_timer_wheel_init, h2o_timer_wheel_get_wake_at, h2o_timer_create, h2o_timer_is_linked, h2o_timer_del, and h2o_timer_wheel__run_, none of which H0 invokes directly from fuzz-controlled operations."],"recommended_action":"Add a stateful timer fuzz target that interprets input as operations over multiple h2o_timer_t objects: initialize a wheel, add timers with arbitrary h2o_timer_abs_t and h2o_timer_val_t values, delete and re-add linked timers, advance or repeat now values across wheel boundaries, run callbacks that reschedule or delete timers, and query h2o_timer_wheel_get_wake_at. Build corresponding coverage for both the native event-loop implementation and H2O_USE_LIBUV."}
